-- coa15-ch6.l4: Part 18, Chapter 6 (Treasury shares), ss 724 to 732 (lines 9523-9616 of ukpga-2006-46.txt).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively, with no seat. Chapter 4's module imports this one (s 706 asks whether s 724 applies); this module
-- takes "the purchase was made in accordance with Chapter 4" as a plain fact. Reading a result: as in coa15-ch1.l4.

DECLARE `s 724(4) act in Chapter 6` IS ONE OF
    `s 724(4) be entered in its register of members as the member holding the shares`
    `s 726(2) exercise a right in respect of the treasury shares`
    `s 727(4) sell or transfer the shares to which the notice relates to a person other than the person who gave the notice`
    `s 728(1) deliver a return to the registrar of the shares sold or transferred for the purposes of an employees' share scheme`
    `s 730(1) deliver a return to the registrar of the shares cancelled`

-- ---- s 724: treasury shares ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9525 | (1) This section applies where–
-- src:9526 | (a) a limited company makes a purchase of its own shares in accordance with Chapter 4, and
-- src:9527 | (b) the purchase is made out of distributable profits.
@ref s 724(1) This section applies where a limited company makes a purchase of its own shares in accordance with Chapter 4 out of distributable profits (src:9525-9527)
GIVEN `a limited company makes a purchase of its own shares in accordance with Chapter 4` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purchase is made out of distributable profits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 724(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF `a limited company makes a purchase of its own shares in accordance with Chapter 4` AND `the purchase is made out of distributable profits`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where– (a) a limited company makes a purchase of its own shares in accordance with Chapter 4, and (b) the purchase is made out of distributable profits."

DECLARE `s 724(3) what the company does with the shares` IS ONE OF
    `s 724(3)(a) hold the shares`
    `s 724(3)(b) deal with the shares in accordance with section 727 or 729`
    `s 724(3) deal with the shares in another way`

-- src:9529 | (3) Where this section applies the company may—
-- src:9530 | (a) hold the shares (or any of them), or
-- src:9531 | (b) deal with any of them, at any time, in accordance with section 727 or 729.
@ref s 724(3) Where this section applies the company may hold the shares or deal with them in accordance with section 727 or 729 (src:9529-9531)
GIVEN `s 724(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      does IS A `s 724(3) what the company does with the shares`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 724(3) the company may do it with the shares` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 724(1) this section applies`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where this section applies the company may"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 724 applies is not known
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
         CONSIDER does
         WHEN `s 724(3) deal with the shares in another way` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) hold the shares (or any of them), or (b) deal with any of them, at any time, in accordance with section 727 or 729"
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:9532 | (4) Where shares are held by the company, the company must be entered in its register of members ... as the member holding the shares.
@ref s 724(4) Where shares are held by the company, the company must be entered in its register of members as the member holding the shares (src:9532-9532)
GIVEN `the shares are held by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 724(4) the company must be entered in its register of members as the member holding the shares` MEANS
    IF `the shares are held by the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where shares are held by the company"

@ref s 724(4) Where shares are held by the company, the company must be entered in its register of members as the member holding the shares (src:9532-9532)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 724(4) act in Chapter 6`
`s 724(4) the company must be entered in its register of members` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 724(4) be entered in its register of members as the member holding the shares`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 724(4): the company was not entered in its register of members as the member holding the shares"

-- src:9533 | (5) In the Companies Acts references to a company holding shares as treasury shares are to the company holding shares that—
-- src:9534 | (a) were (or are treated as having been) purchased by it in circumstances in which this section applies, and
-- src:9535 | (b) have been held by the company continuously since they were so purchased (or treated as purchased).
@ref s 724(5) References to a company holding shares as treasury shares (src:9533-9535)
GIVEN `the shares were (or are treated as having been) purchased by the company in circumstances in which section 724 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares have been held by the company continuously since they were so purchased (or treated as purchased)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 724(5) the company holds the shares as treasury shares` MEANS
    IF `the shares were (or are treated as having been) purchased by the company in circumstances in which section 724 applies`
       AND `the shares have been held by the company continuously since they were so purchased (or treated as purchased)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "references to a company holding shares as treasury shares are to the company holding shares that— (a) were (or are treated as having been) purchased by it in circumstances in which this section applies, and (b) have been held by the company continuously since they were so purchased"

