DECLARE `s 727(1) disposal` IS ONE OF
    `s 727(1)(a) a sale of the shares for a cash consideration`
    `s 727(1)(b) a transfer of the shares for the purposes of or pursuant to an employees' share scheme`
    `s 727(1) any other disposal`

-- src:9548 | (1) Where shares are held as treasury shares, the company may at any time—
-- src:9549 | (a) sell the shares (or any of them) for a cash consideration, or
-- src:9550 | (b) transfer the shares (or any of them) for the purposes of or pursuant to an employees' share scheme.
@ref s 727(1) Where shares are held as treasury shares, the company may at any time sell them for a cash consideration or transfer them for an employees' share scheme (src:9548-9550)
GIVEN `shares are held as treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      disposal IS A `s 727(1) disposal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 727(1) the company may dispose of the shares in that way` MEANS
    IF (NOT `shares are held as treasury shares`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where shares are held as treasury shares, the company may at any time"
    ELSE CONSIDER disposal
         WHEN `s 727(1) any other disposal` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text names a sale for a cash consideration and a transfer for an employees' share scheme and does not close the list
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 727(2) kind of consideration` IS ONE OF
    `s 727(2)(a) cash received by the company`
    `s 727(2)(b) a cheque received by the company` HAS `s 727(2)(b) received in good faith, and the directors have no reason for suspecting that it will not be paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 727(2)(c) a release of a liability of the company for a liquidated sum`
    `s 727(2)(d) an undertaking to pay cash to the company` HAS `s 727(2)(d) days after the date on which the company agrees to sell the shares by which the cash is to be paid` IS A NUMBER
    `s 727(2)(e) payment by any other means giving rise to a present or future entitlement to a payment, or credit equivalent to payment, in cash`
    `s 727(2) any other consideration`

-- src:9551 | (2) In subsection (1)(a) “cash consideration” means—
-- src:9552 | (a) cash received by the company, or
-- src:9553 | (b) a cheque received by the company in good faith that the directors have no reason for suspecting will not be paid, or
-- src:9554 | (c) a release of a liability of the company for a liquidated sum, or
-- src:9555 | (d) an undertaking to pay cash to the company on or before a date not more than 90 days after the date on which the company agrees to sell the shares, or
-- src:9556 | (e) payment by any other means giving rise to a present or future entitlement (of the company or a person acting on the company's behalf) to a payment, or credit equivalent to payment, in cash.
@ref s 727(2) "cash consideration" means cash, a cheque, a release, an undertaking to pay cash within 90 days, or payment by any other means giving rise to an entitlement to cash (src:9551-9556)
GIVEN consideration IS A `s 727(2) kind of consideration`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 727(2) the consideration is a cash consideration` MEANS
    CONSIDER consideration
    WHEN `s 727(2)(a) cash received by the company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 727(2)(b) a cheque received by the company` good THEN
         IF good THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“cash consideration” means— ... (b) a cheque received by the company in good faith that the directors have no reason for suspecting will not be paid"
    WHEN `s 727(2)(c) a release of a liability of the company for a liquidated sum` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 727(2)(d) an undertaking to pay cash to the company` days THEN
         IF days AT MOST 90
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an undertaking to pay cash to the company on or before a date not more than 90 days after the date on which the company agrees to sell the shares"
    WHEN `s 727(2)(e) payment by any other means giving rise to a present or future entitlement to a payment, or credit equivalent to payment, in cash` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 727(2) any other consideration` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“cash consideration” means— (a) ... (e) ..."

-- src:9557 | For this purpose “cash” includes foreign currency.
@ref s 727(2) "cash" includes foreign currency (src:9557-9557)
GIVEN `the money is foreign currency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 727(2) the money is cash` MEANS
    IF `the money is foreign currency`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "For this purpose “cash” includes foreign currency."

