GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 727(4) the sale or transfer is barred` MEANS
    IF `the company has received a notice under section 979 that a person desires to acquire shares held by the company as treasury shares` AND (NOT `the sale or transfer is to that person`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the company receives a notice under section 979 ... the company must not sell or transfer the shares to which the notice relates except to that person"

@ref s 727(4) If the company receives a notice under section 979, it must not sell or transfer the shares to which the notice relates except to that person (src:9559-9559)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 724(4) act in Chapter 6`
`s 727(4) the company shant sell or transfer the shares except to the person who gave the notice` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    SHANT `s 727(4) sell or transfer the shares to which the notice relates to a person other than the person who gave the notice`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 727(4): the company sold or transferred shares to which a section 979 notice relates to someone other than the person who gave it"

