-- src:9566 | (2) The return must state with respect to shares of each class disposed of—
-- src:9567 | (a) the number and nominal value of the shares, and
-- src:9568 | (b) the date on which they were disposed of.
@ref s 728(2) The return must state, for shares of each class disposed of, the number and nominal value and the date of disposal (src:9566-9568)
GIVEN entries IS A LIST OF `s 728(2) class entry`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 728(2) the return states what the section requires` MEANS
    -- fork F-empty-list: with no class entry in the facts the answer is NOTHING: the facts do not say that shares of any class were disposed of
    CONSIDER entries
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the facts give no class entry, so they do not say whether the company disposed of shares of a class
    OTHERWISE
        IF all (GIVEN e YIELD (e's `s 728(2) states the number and nominal value of the shares of the class disposed of`) AND (e's `s 728(2) states the date on which they were disposed of`)) entries
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The return must state with respect to shares of each class disposed of— (a) the number and nominal value of the shares, and (b) the date on which they were disposed of." (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)

