-- src:9570 | (4) If default is made in complying with this section an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 728(4) Offence (src:9570-9570)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 728` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 658(2) person charged`
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 728(4) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    -- fork F-not-in-default: an officer who is not in default is answered NOTHING (the text charges only officers in default); the other reading answers JUST FALSE
    IF (NOT `default is made in complying with section 728`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with this section"
    ELSE CONSIDER person
         WHEN `s 658(2) the company` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text charges every officer of the company who is in default
         WHEN `s 658(2) an officer of the company` THEN
              CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who is in default"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is in default is s 1121 (coa24)
         WHEN `s 658(2) a director of the company` THEN
              CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who is in default"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is in default is s 1121 (coa24)
         OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text charges every officer of the company who is in default

-- The text shows two wordings of the daily default fine run together ("one-tenth of the statutory maximumone-tenth of the greater of
-- £5,000 or the amount corresponding to level 4 on the standard scale for summary offences"): see F-penalty in NOTES.md. The function takes which
-- wording is in force as an input and answers NOTHING when it is not known.
-- src:9571 | (5) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:9572 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:9573 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of the statutory maximumone-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or the amount corresponding to level 4 on the standard scale for summary offences.
@ref s 728(5) Penalty on conviction (src:9571-9573)
GIVEN how IS A `Mode of conviction`
      `the wording that substitutes the greater of £5,000 and the level 4 amount is in force` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 707(7) penalty`
`s 728(5) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    -- fork F-penalty: the text shows two wordings of the daily default fine run together; which is in force is an input, and NOTHING when it is not known
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST (`s 707(7) penalty` OF `on conviction on indictment`, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN `s 728(5) the summary penalty` how `the wording that substitutes the greater of £5,000 and the level 4 amount is in force`
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN `s 728(5) the summary penalty` how `the wording that substitutes the greater of £5,000 and the level 4 amount is in force`
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN `s 728(5) the summary penalty` how `the wording that substitutes the greater of £5,000 and the level 4 amount is in force`
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN `s 728(5) the summary penalty` how `the wording that substitutes the greater of £5,000 and the level 4 amount is in force`
    WHERE
        `s 728(5) the summary penalty` how2 amended MEANS
            CONSIDER amended
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
                 JUST (`s 707(7) penalty` OF how2, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), JUST (`s 707(7) one-tenth of the greater of an amount in pounds and the amount corresponding to a level on the standard scale` 5000 4))
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
                 JUST (`s 707(7) penalty` OF how2, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), JUST `s 707(7) one-tenth of the statutory maximum`)
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text shows both wordings and does not say which is in force

