    `s 730(2) states the number and nominal value of the shares of the class cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 730(2) states the date on which they were cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:9581 | (1) Where shares held by a company as treasury shares are cancelled, the company must deliver a return to the registrar not later than 28 days after the shares are cancelled.
-- src:9582 | This does not apply to shares that are cancelled forthwith on their acquisition by the company (see section 708).
@ref s 730(1) Where treasury shares are cancelled, the company must deliver a return not later than 28 days after the shares are cancelled (not shares cancelled forthwith on acquisition) (src:9581-9582)
GIVEN `the date on which the shares were cancelled` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 730(1) the last day for delivering the return to the registrar` MEANS `the date on which the shares were cancelled` PLUS 28

@ref s 730(1) Where treasury shares are cancelled, the company must deliver a return not later than 28 days after the shares are cancelled (not shares cancelled forthwith on acquisition) (src:9581-9582)
GIVEN `the shares are cancelled forthwith on their acquisition by the company (see section 708)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the shares were cancelled` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the company delivered the return to the registrar` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 730(1) the return was delivered not later than 28 days after the shares were cancelled` MEANS
    IF `the shares are cancelled forthwith on their acquisition by the company (see section 708)`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This does not apply to shares that are cancelled forthwith on their acquisition by the company (see section 708)": section 708 deals with them
    ELSE IF `the date on which the company delivered the return to the registrar` AT LEAST `the date on which the shares were cancelled`
            AND `the date on which the company delivered the return to the registrar` AT MOST (`s 730(1) the last day for delivering the return to the registrar` `the date on which the shares were cancelled`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must deliver a return to the registrar not later than 28 days after the shares are cancelled"

@ref s 730(1) Where treasury shares are cancelled, the company must deliver a return not later than 28 days after the shares are cancelled (not shares cancelled forthwith on acquisition) (src:9581-9582)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 724(4) act in Chapter 6`
`s 730(1) the company must deliver a return to the registrar` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 730(1) deliver a return to the registrar of the shares cancelled`
    WITHIN 28
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 730(1): the return was not delivered to the registrar not later than 28 days after the shares were cancelled"

-- src:9583 | (2) The return must state with respect to shares of each class cancelled—
-- src:9584 | (a) the number and nominal value of the shares, and
-- src:9585 | (b) the date on which they were cancelled.
