GIVEN entries IS A LIST OF `s 730(2) class entry`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 730(2) the return states what the section requires` MEANS
    -- fork F-empty-list: with no class entry in the facts the answer is NOTHING: the facts do not say that shares of any class were cancelled
    CONSIDER entries
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the facts give no class entry, so they do not say whether the company cancelled shares of a class
    OTHERWISE
        IF all (GIVEN e YIELD (e's `s 730(2) states the number and nominal value of the shares of the class cancelled`) AND (e's `s 730(2) states the date on which they were cancelled`)) entries
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The return must state with respect to shares of each class cancelled— (a) the number and nominal value of the shares, and (b) the date on which they were cancelled." (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)

