GIVEN `shares held as treasury shares are sold` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 731(1) this section applies to the proceeds of sale` MEANS
    IF `shares held as treasury shares are sold`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where shares held as treasury shares are sold, the proceeds of sale must be dealt with in accordance with this section"

-- src:9602 | (1) Where shares held as treasury shares are sold, the proceeds of sale must be dealt with in accordance with this section.
-- src:9603 | (2) If the proceeds of sale are equal to or less than the purchase price paid by the company for the shares, the proceeds are treated for the purposes of Part 23 (distributions) as a realised profit of the company.
@ref s 731(2) If the proceeds of sale are equal to or less than the purchase price, the proceeds are treated as a realised profit (src:9602-9603)
GIVEN `the proceeds of sale` IS A NUMBER
      `the purchase price paid by the company for the shares` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 731(2) the amount treated as a realised profit of the company for the purposes of Part 23` MEANS
    IF `the proceeds of sale` AT MOST `the purchase price paid by the company for the shares`
    THEN JUST `the proceeds of sale`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the proceeds of sale are equal to or less than the purchase price paid by the company for the shares": subsection (3) decides the other case

-- src:9604 | (3) If the proceeds of sale exceed the purchase price paid by the company—
-- src:9605 | (a) an amount equal to the purchase price paid is treated as a realised profit of the company for the purposes of that Part, and
@ref s 731(3)(a) If the proceeds of sale exceed the purchase price, an amount equal to the purchase price is treated as a realised profit (src:9604-9605)
GIVEN `the proceeds of sale` IS A NUMBER
      `the purchase price paid by the company for the shares` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 731(3)(a) the amount treated as a realised profit of the company` MEANS
    IF `the proceeds of sale` GREATER THAN `the purchase price paid by the company for the shares`
    THEN JUST `the purchase price paid by the company for the shares`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the proceeds of sale exceed the purchase price paid by the company": subsection (2) decides the other case

-- src:9604 | (3) If the proceeds of sale exceed the purchase price paid by the company—
-- src:9605 | (a) an amount equal to the purchase price paid is treated as a realised profit of the company for the purposes of that Part, and
-- src:9606 | (b) the excess must be transferred to the company's share premium account.
@ref s 731(3)(b) The excess must be transferred to the company's share premium account (src:9604-9606)
GIVEN `the proceeds of sale` IS A NUMBER
      `the purchase price paid by the company for the shares` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 731(3)(b) the amount to be transferred to the company's share premium account` MEANS
    IF `the proceeds of sale` GREATER THAN `the purchase price paid by the company for the shares`
    THEN JUST (`the proceeds of sale` MINUS `the purchase price paid by the company for the shares`)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the proceeds of sale exceed the purchase price paid by the company"

-- src:9607 | (4) For the purposes of this section—
-- src:9608 | (a) the purchase price paid by the company must be determined by the application of a weighted average price method, and
@ref s 731(4)(a) The purchase price paid by the company must be determined by a weighted average price method (src:9607-9608)
GIVEN `the total purchase price paid for all the treasury shares of the class held` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of treasury shares of the class held` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of shares sold` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 731(4)(a) the purchase price paid by the company for the shares sold` MEANS
    -- fork F-weighted: the text names "a weighted average price method" without defining it; the plain weighted average over the class held is taken, and NOTHING where no shares are held; another method (a moving average, say) would give another price
    IF `the number of treasury shares of the class held` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN JUST ((`the total purchase price paid for all the treasury shares of the class held` DIVIDED BY `the number of treasury shares of the class held`) TIMES `the number of shares sold`)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): a weighted average price method is not defined, and with no shares held it has no meaning; the text says only that the price paid must be determined by it

-- src:9607 | (4) For the purposes of this section—
-- src:9608 | (a) the purchase price paid by the company must be determined by the application of a weighted average price method, and
-- src:9609 | (b) if the shares were allotted to the company as fully paid bonus shares, the purchase price paid for them is treated as nil.
@ref s 731(4)(b) If the shares were allotted as fully paid bonus shares, the purchase price paid for them is treated as nil (src:9607-9609)
GIVEN `the shares were allotted to the company as fully paid bonus shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 731(4)(b) the purchase price paid for the shares` MEANS
    IF `the shares were allotted to the company as fully paid bonus shares`
    THEN JUST 0
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the shares were allotted to the company as fully paid bonus shares": paragraph (a) decides the other case

-- ---- s 732: offences ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9611 | (1) If a company contravenes any of the provisions of this Chapter (except section 730 (notice of cancellation)), an offence is committed by—
-- src:9612 | (a) the company, and
-- src:9613 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 732(1) Offence (src:9611-9613)
GIVEN `the company contravenes a provision of Chapter 6 other than section 730` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 658(2) person charged`
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 732(1) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    -- fork F-not-in-default: an officer who is not in default is answered NOTHING (the text charges only officers in default); the other reading answers JUST FALSE
    IF (NOT `the company contravenes a provision of Chapter 6 other than section 730`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company contravenes any of the provisions of this Chapter (except section 730 (notice of cancellation))"
    ELSE CONSIDER person
         WHEN `s 658(2) the company` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 658(2) an officer of the company` THEN
              CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who is in default"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is in default is s 1121 (coa24)
         WHEN `s 658(2) a director of the company` THEN
              CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who is in default"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is in default is s 1121 (coa24)
         OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text charges the company and every officer of the company who is in default

-- src:9614 | (2) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:9615 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:9616 | (b) on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 732(2) Penalty on conviction (src:9614-9616)
GIVEN how IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 732(2) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    -- Penalty OF  how convicted,  imprisonment not exceeding,  fine not exceeding,  daily default fine,  imprisonment and fine together
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
